<title>USA: OUTLOOK - US ag exports $55.5 bln in FY97 - USDA f'cst.</title>
<headline>OUTLOOK - US ag exports $55.5 bln in FY97 - USDA f'cst.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1997-02-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Agriculture Department forecast Monday U.S. farm exports would total $55.5 billion this fiscal year, down from a record $59.8 billion last year.</p>
<p>&quot;Much of the record fiscal 1996 export value reflected high bulk commodity prices for grains and oilseeds,&quot; USDA said in the forecast made as part of its annual Outlook Forum.</p>
<p>With lower prices, the value of U.S. exports will decline, USDA said, but begin a steady rise in 1998 and hitting record levels before the end of the decade. Imports would not rise as quickly, so the agriculture trade surplus would widen.</p>
<p> (Bln $)			  FY1997  FY1998</p>
<p> Animals and products	  11.5    12.4</p>
<p> Grains, feed and products   21.3    16.2</p>
<p> Oilseeds and products	  9.7     9.8</p>
<p> Horticultural products	10.2    10.7</p>
<p> Unmanf'd tobacco		 1.4     1.4</p>
<p> Cotton and linters	     3.0     2.1</p>
<p> Other				2.7     2.9</p>
<p> Total agricultural exports  59.8    55.5</p>
<p> Bulk comodities		 27.9    22.0</p>
<p> High-value products	   31.9    33.5</p>
<p> Total agricultural imports  32.4    34.0</p>
<p> Net ag trade surplus	  27.4    21.5</p>
</text>
